WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.834
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:03.934
Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.000
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.901
I appreciate it.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.200
Let's get to some news.
Well, guys,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.634
the FDA just announced that

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:13.067
the U.S. has less
than two months to decide

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:17.300
whether Americans need
COVID booster shots this fall.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.734
Yeah, but don't worry,
whatever they decide,

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.267
they promise
to roll out the new rules

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.734
in the most confusing way
possible.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
Honestly, at this point,

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.801
how do we not have
Vaccine Prime?

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:28.801
Well, earlier this week,

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.100
former President Obama
visited the White House.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.968
Did you see that?

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.133
And everyone went nuts for him.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.434
[ Laughter ]
Almost too crazy, yeah.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.200
They just wouldn't
stop clapping.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.334
[ Laughter ]
And Biden was like,

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.267
"Okay, we're good."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.534
But then he gave an address

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.467
that really boosted morale
and I think it's even

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.868
rubbing off on President Biden.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:48.400
Listen to the speech
that Biden gave today. Listen.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.868
-[ As Obama ]
Uh, okay, look,

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.367
there's too much, uh,

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.934
malarkey in Washington.

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.400
[ Laughter ]
I'm still committed to passing

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.801
[ Staccato ]
my Build Back Better plan.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.267
[ Staccato ]
Build Back Better.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:01.234
You know, my mom used to, uh,
she'd sit me down.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.534
She'd say, "Joey."

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:06.467
She'd say, "Don't take no rubber
pennies from nobody."

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:07.868
[ Laughter ]
But let me be clear, Jack.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.200
I'd like to announce also
that I'm changing my name

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.534
from Joe Biden to just Obiden.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.434
[ Laughter ]
I like that.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:14.734
President Obiden.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:15.734
Go, trains!

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:18.100
-Yeah, wow, go, trains.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.200
[ Cheering and applause ]
Obiden.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.400
-Obiden, like Obama.
-He wants to go by

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.901
President Obiden.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.601
-I like it, yeah.
That's good.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.601
Guys, some entertainment news --
it was just announced

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:28.067
that Chip and Joanna Gaines'
Magnolia Network

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.601
is moving to HBO.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.033
[ Oohing ]

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.601
-That should be great.
Now, they can finally show

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:35.100
all the profanity when a couple
fights over cabinet knobs.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.467
Speaking of HBO, I read
that they're is planning

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:42.100
to create a Sherlock Holmes
TV Universe.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.200
[ Oohs, smattering of applause ]

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.634
So, between this
and Chip and Joanna,

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.267
HBO really seems to be
into shows about ho(l)mes.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:52.434
[ Laughter and slow clap ]

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:53.667
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.667
[ The Roots playing
mellow funk ]

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:03.634
♪♪

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:06.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:07.701
Ooh!
-Wow.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.534
-Yeah.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.767
And the Emmy goes to...

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.667
Listen to this --
amid high oil price,

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.968
American Airlines is going
to use a bus service

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.934
as an alternative to some

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.400
[ Laughter ]
short connecting flights.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.534
A bus, instead of a plane.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:26.367
It's the equivalent of a waiter
saying, "We're out of Coke.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.434
Is backwash okay?"

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.300
[ Laughter and ewws ]

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.534
On the bright side, at least
there won't be a security line,

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.501
since pretty much anything goes
on a bus.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.567
[ Laughter ]
I think it's actually
a smart idea.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.501
American Airlines is like,
"Oil prices are high,

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.534
but thank God
gas prices are low.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.234
Bus it is!
No one reads the news."

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.033
Speaking of flights,
a former British Airways pilot

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:46.801
who lied about his
flying experience

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.934
has been sentenced
to a year in jail

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:52.734
after he pressed a button
"no qualified pilot would."

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:56.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.334
Maybe I'm crazy, but if there's
a button in the cockpit

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.400
you should never press,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.000
maybe don't put it on the plane,
you know?

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.534
[ As Obama ]
Don't -- Don't
put it on the plane.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.567
And, finally,
I heard about a woman in Texas

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.868
who just finished running
her 1,000th marathon.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:19.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.133
Even her FitBit was like,
"Okay, we get it."

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.167
[ Laughter ]
At this point,
her friends are like,

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:24.801
"Cheryl, what are you
running from?"

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show.

